63F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"kRG2ZrCT5RvwD2tajVnpjA","review_id":"7VNvultCcZB_WdPc_bXqAw","date":"2014-03-26T22:00:43","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9504044055938721,"text_excerpt":"Confession time again, as a teenager we all go through stages and phases. Well I went through my rock, metal and goth stage...yes I was pretty hardcore at one time. Three or 4 years ago (give or take, during a girls only trip) while walking along Bourbon St. I saw a sign, under the sign was a black door being carefully guarded by black haired, spiked jeweled collars and bracelets wearing individuals. Echoes of pain emanated from within and the thudding and pounding took hold of me like an invisible force pulling me in, calling to me. I stepped inside the door and made my way through a tight and narrow pathway, dark smelling of sulfur. At the end I entered a room where the walls were paint..."},{"business_id":"kRG2ZrCT5RvwD2tajVnpjA","review_id":"o-cK1behKVtCTs-TqZZqEQ","date":"2017-09-28T00:10:23","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9356931447982788,"text_excerpt":"Yo I love The Dungeon! It's a nice little escape from Bourbon Street vibes. Walk down a spooky little alley into a cloud of fog and heavy metal music to find a gothic oasis inside. Sit in the cage upstairs or hang out in the coffin. I like to take people on first dates here so they know how weird I am right from the beginning. Maybe that's why I am still single? Oh well, I have way too much fun there! All the bartenders that I have encountered are always super nice and I feel like the security guys always got my back. They seem really actually care that everyone in there is safe. Don't do anything too stupid like dancing on the cage or stumbling around too drunk because the boys are watch..."},{"business_id":"kRG2ZrCT5RvwD2tajVnpjA","review_id":"r40kCoudxVgq2iJDpdUnLw","date":"2016-01-13T19:18:35","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9350622296333313,"text_excerpt":"Without a friend's recommendation, I probably would have skipped right over the Dungeon. Literally. It's located on Toulouse off of Bourbon and you need to walk down an alley to get in. The vibe is dark and ominous. No photos allowed. No outside drinks allowed. I don't recommend chugging your grenade for the obvious reason of having to chug a grenade then needing to throw out your souvenir glass. Once I learned the rules, this bar skyrocketed to the top of the bars I went to on my recent NOLA trip. My friend and I sat at the front bar near the fish tank. They don't have a menu so we took our bartender suggestion on beverages. We went with the Witches Brew which was amaretto based and tast..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"kRG2ZrCT5RvwD2tajVnpjA","photo_id":"eouHcwXOjSgi_8N83eiSzw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/eouHcwXOjSgi_8N83eiSzw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9470422863960266},{"business_id":"kRG2ZrCT5RvwD2tajVnpjA","photo_id":"sHGKH5qdLhUK6HmCFHivTg"